# hakai — suggested Hyprland keybinds.
#
# Not applied automatically by the package (editing a user's own dotfiles from a package
# install is the kind of thing that should never happen silently) — copy whatever you want
# into your own ~/.config/hypr/bindings.conf instead.
#
# SUPER SHIFT H is what this project itself uses — chosen after SUPER SHIFT D, Omarchy's
# own default keybind (matching its usual "SUPER SHIFT + first letter" app-launcher
# pattern) turned out to already be bound to LazyDocker on a real Omarchy install. Check
# `Super K` (Omarchy's own live keybindings reference) before relying on H being free on
# your own machine too, since Omarchy's default bindings have changed across its major
# versions.
bindd = SUPER SHIFT, H, Destroy the desktop, exec, uwsm app -- hakai
bindd = SUPER SHIFT ALT, H, Stop destroying it, exec, pkill -x hakai
